        <general_population_average>70-80 bpm (typical resting HR for adults)</general_population_average>
        <athlete_range>40-60 bpm (often lower due to cardiovascular fitness)</athlete_range>
        <interpretation_framework>
          User's current 68 bpm is:
          - POPULATION: Clinically normal (within 60-100 bpm healthy range) and below general population average (70-80 bpm)
          - PERSONAL: 8 bpm above user's baseline (60 bpm), indicating stress/sleep-deprivation response
          - SLEEP CAUSATION (V2): Last night's poor sleep (6h, quality 62, deep sleep 10.5%) is driving today's elevation
          - SYNTHESIS: "You're fundamentally healthier than average—your baseline is better than most people's. But poor sleep is elevating you from YOUR optimal state. The good news: improving sleep can return you to a baseline that's better than where most people start."
        </interpretation_framework>
      </heart_rate>

